(:id "port/python/packet/unions" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/python/python_packet_unions_test.go: TestPythonPacketUnions" "make packet-void-python (make/python.mk)" "internal/codegen/python/python_packet_unions_test.go: TestPythonPacketUnionsNegativeControl" "make packet-void-python-negative-control (make/python.mk)") :tested-revision "af344f3049bed95aa350a7eb3b325192e3dc861c" :note "2026-11-15: test/packet-void/python/Python.schema carries tagged unions of type payloads (Mixed.payload) and named payload-free arms (Mixed.ping, Mixed.pong) beside Tags, Single, Empty and the bool-framed Frame; python/goldens.txt is the hand-calculated SPEC §4.8 wire and every case reads and writes back byte for byte under CPython 3.11.18 (floor) and 3.15.2 (current). The probe checks the tag classes and slot layout, that every payload arm is born at its declared default and rebuilt before decoding, that out-of-contract writes (tag, payload type, int range, bool) raise InvalidValue and truncated or hostile input raises Refused. TestPythonPacketUnionsNegativeControl plants one extra set bit on a payload-free arm's write in a copy of the generated code and the probe goes red by name. Run on Linux x86_64 with the pinned interpreters from make dist-python, SCHEMA_SLOW=1, mypy 1.18.2 --strict --python-version 3.11 over the generated tree, at this revision.")
(:id "port/python/packet/payload-free-arms" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/python/python_packet_unions_test.go: TestPythonPacketUnions" "make packet-void-python (make/python.mk)" "internal/codegen/python/python_packet_unions_test.go: TestPythonPacketUnionsNegativeControl" "make packet-void-python-negative-control (make/python.mk)") :tested-revision "af344f3049bed95aa350a7eb3b325192e3dc861c" :note "2026-11-15: the Python half of test/packet-void holds every named payload-free arm to exactly its tag bits: Mixed None/Ping/Pong and Tags None/Pong write and read 0x00, 0x01, 0x03 and 0x02, Single Ack 0x01 in one bit, Empty None writes no bits, and Frame puts a payload-free tag between two one-bit bools as 0x0B. The union class carries only the tag and one attribute per payload arm, every payload arm built at construction, so reading a void arm still leaves its payload at the declared defaults. Invalid tags, a bool where a tag is declared, missing tag input and trailing bytes raise InvalidValue or Refused. The negative control spends one extra set bit on a payload-free arm's write in a copy of the generated code and the exact write marker goes red. Run on Linux x86_64 under CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2 from make dist-python, SCHEMA_SLOW=1, with mypy --strict over the generated tree, at this revision.")
